+# Contract: Rustdoc Attachment and Diff Discipline
+
+**Feature**: [../spec.md](../spec.md) · **Applies to**: `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs`,
+`apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs`
+
+This feature has no wire, CLI-surface, or storage interface change; its observable interface is
+(a) the documented text each of four functions renders (the promise users of hover help / rustdoc
+read) and (b) the shape of the change itself (FR-004). Both are contracted here.
+
+## 1. Documented-text contract (post-change, SC-001)
+
+The rendered documentation of each named item MUST equal the following, line for line, with no
+additional text. Blocks are identified by their first and last lines (sentinels from
+[../data-model.md](../data-model.md)); interior lines are fixed by FR-005 (verbatim, pre-existing).
+
+| Item | Module | Rendered documentation MUST | Rendered documentation MUST NOT |
+|------|--------|------------------------------|---------------------------------|
+| `addressable_scope` | `commands::execution` | Begin with "The ONE scope the `execution` verbs can address for a given execution id.", contain the full body, and end with the `# Errors` subsection whose last line is "``[`Failure`] when `execution` is not a valid identifier.`" | Contain any line of `repository_scope`'s block (no "same addressing rule … records that belong to the local repository" text; no Dreams shadow ledger reference; no "two constructions cannot drift apart") |
+| `repository_scope` | `commands::execution` | Be exactly its own 3-line block: "The same addressing rule as [`addressable_scope`] for records that belong to the local repository rather than to one execution stream (for example the Dreams shadow ledger). One home for the workspace and project literals, so the two constructions cannot drift apart." | Contain any line of `addressable_scope`'s block — in particular no "ONE scope" text, no "# Errors" heading, no failure contract (the function takes no parameter and cannot fail) |
+| `assign_schema` | `commands::mcp::tools` | Nothing (zero doc-comment lines attached) | Contain "`fixture` and `route` are both optional", the "exactly one door" rule text, or any line of `synthesize_schema`'s block |
+| `synthesize_schema` | `commands::mcp::tools` | Be exactly the 4-line block beginning "Closed like every other schema here. `fixture` and `route` are both optional and the route refuses the pair…" and ending "…for the same reason `start_schema` does not encode file-or-graph." | Contain borrowed text about `assign`'s fields (`node`, `actorId`) — none exists in the source, so none may appear |
+
+All other items in both files keep exactly the documentation they had at baseline head `25b34ed`
+(SC-003 second half).
+
+## 2. Reference-resolution contract (FR-006, SC-003)
+
+Intra-doc links inside moved blocks must resolve to the same targets as before the move:
+
+| Link | Occurs in | Target | Target location after fix | Resolvable? |
+|------|-----------|--------|---------------------------|-------------|
+| `` [`Failure`] `` | moved execution block | `Failure` struct | same module, `execution/mod.rs` (declared at baseline line 80) | Yes — unchanged |
+| `` [`addressable_scope`] `` | moved execution block AND staying 3-line block | `addressable_scope` fn | same module, now directly below its own block | Yes — unchanged scope |
+| backtick spans `serve::routes:: synthesize`, `start_schema` | moved tools.rs block | plain code spans, not intra-doc links | n/a (no link resolution involved) | Yes — unchanged |
+
+No new links are introduced or removed by the change.
+
+## 3. Diff-shape contract (FR-004, FR-005, SC-002)
+
+Against the pre-change tree, the delivered change MUST satisfy all of:
+
+1. `git status --porcelain` lists no modified path other than the two files above (feature
+   artifacts under `specs/001-bench/` and `.specify/` excluded as pipeline output, not part of the
+   source change).
+2. Every added or removed content line matches `^[+-]\s*///`; zero non-comment lines differ.
+3. The multiset of removed comment lines equals the multiset of added comment lines (a pure
+   permutation): per file, 11 removed == 11 added in `execution/mod.rs`, 4 removed == 4 added in
+   `mcp/tools.rs`.
+4. No blank line is added or removed anywhere; the hunks reposition whole contiguous runs only.
+5. Line endings normalize to LF for both `.rs` paths (`.gitattributes`: `*.rs text eol=lf`).
