+
+# Tasks: Restore Displaced Documentation Comments
+
+**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-bench/`
+
+**Prerequisites**: plan.md (required), spec.md (required for user stories), research.md, data-model.md, contracts/rustdoc-attachment.md, quickstart.md — all present in `specs/001-bench/`.
+
+**Governance substitution (recorded)**: this checkout has no `/memory/constitution.md`; per the run
+instructions the repository-root `AGENTS.md` is used as the governance reference here (also spec A5).
+`.specify/extensions.yml` does not exist, so **all extension hooks (pre- and post-tasks) are skipped**.
+
+**Baseline head**: every line number below refers to clean baseline head `25b34ed` (confirmed at task
+generation: `git rev-parse --short HEAD` = `25b34ed`; only untracked paths are `.specify/` and `specs/`).
+
+**Tests**: Not requested. The spec states no runtime behavior changes (A4) and research R5 rejects new
+automated tests as proxies that would freeze incidental source spelling/positions. Each story is verified
+by **observation** of the rendered/documented text and the diff (quickstart Scenarios 1–5), not by new
+unit/integration test files. There are therefore no "Tests for User Story N" subsections.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
+
+- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependency on an incomplete task)
+- **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (US1, US2, US3)
+- Exact file paths are included in every description.
+
+## Path Conventions
+
+Single Rust workspace; both edits are intra-file comment relocations inside the existing
+`graphhelm-cli` crate. The only two source files touched (FR-004):
+
+- `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs`
+- `apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs`
+
+---
+
+## Phase 1: Setup (Shared Infrastructure)
+
+**Purpose**: No project scaffolding is created — the change edits two existing files in an existing crate.
+This phase confirms a clean baseline and records the "before" measurements that later scenarios assert
+against (before == after). Both tasks are read-only observers; no source bytes change yet.
+
+- [X] T001 Confirm a clean baseline working tree from the repo root with `git status --porcelain`: no modified source path exists and the only untracked paths are `.specify/` and `specs/` (FR-004 baseline precondition — nothing pre-existing to misattribute)
+- [X] T002 Record the "before" measurements (quickstart Step 0) into the working notes: count `^\s*///` lines in `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs` and in `apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs`, and capture `git diff --numstat` (expected empty); keep the two per-file counts — Scenario 3 asserts they are unchanged after the edits
+
+**Checkpoint**: Baseline head confirmed clean; before-measurements recorded for the before == after assertions.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)
+
