+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — can start immediately.
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup completion — **BLOCKS all user stories** (displacement-shape verification + shared invariant).
+- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: Depends on Foundational. No dependency on US2/US3.
+- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: Depends on Foundational. No dependency on US1 — different file, so it may run in parallel with US1.
+- **User Story 3 (Phase 5)**: Depends on US1 **and** US2 (it verifies the whole delivered, two-file change).
+- **Polish (Phase 6)**: Depends on US3 (consolidated acceptance + delivery record).
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **User Story 1 (P1)**: Start after Foundational (Phase 2) — independent of other stories.
+- **User Story 2 (P2)**: Start after Foundational (Phase 2) — independent of US1 (disjoint file), runs in parallel.
+- **User Story 3 (P3)**: Start after US1 and US2 — cross-cutting proof over both files.
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- The implementation task precedes its own-file verification task (same file ⇒ not parallel).
+- No automated tests are written first (none requested; see Tests note) — verification is by quickstart observation of the edited file.
+- Story complete and independently validated before relying on the next story.
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- **Primary**: T004 (US1, `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs`) ∥ T006 (US2, `apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs`) — disjoint files, both unblocked once Phase 2 completes.
+- Secondary (read-only, batchable once US1+US2 land): the four US3 checks T008–T011 are independent observations over the finished diff and can be batched, though they share the two files so they are not flagged [P].
